 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-09",
  "asof": "2026-09-10 09:26 UTC",
  "headline": "Brent broke $100 the day before CPI \u2014 and Phoenix never saw the session",
  "standfirst": "The engine has not run since Wednesday morning. This pack was built at 09:26 UTC, before the US open, so every price in it is Tuesday's: SPX still reads 7,673.52, macro_series ends on the 8th and so does every chart file. There is no Wednesday close, no Wednesday mark and no Wednesday R in this brief, and the PLTR stop condition cannot be checked at all. What is known comes from the press and is labelled: Brent jumped 3.4% back above $100 for the first time since July, Treasury yields set 52-week highs, the S&P closed 0.5% lower at 7,636.36 \u2014 and Apple priced its foldable at $1,999, under what was trailed, closing roughly flat. Heat is unchanged at 4.04R against 3.0R because nothing in the book moved. CPI prints this morning.",
  "themes": [],
  "ondeck": "August CPI lands today, Friday 11 September at 08:30 ET, and is the regime's tightest gate; the Bank of Japan meets next week with a hike 97% priced; the FOMC meets 15\u201316 September; triple witching is 18 September. Tomorrow's brief covers the CPI session and carries the weekly.",
